<code>assert this.get(0).equals(e) && \old(this.size()) + 1 == this.size();</code>

However, the comment specifies "The first position contains the appended element," which seems to imply that the element should be at the first position (index 0) after the append operation. Given the standard behavior of the `add` method, the element is actually appended to the end of the list, not the beginning. Therefore, the correct interpretation should reflect that the element is at the last position.

So the correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert this.get(this.size() - 1).equals(e) && \old(this.size()) + 1 == this.size();</code>
