The comment states that "The first position contains the appended element." However, this is not entirely accurate because the element is appended to the end of the vector, not necessarily the first position. The correct interpretation is that if the vector was empty before the addition, the first position will contain the appended element. Otherwise, the first position will still contain the same element as before. 

To accurately reflect this, the assertion checks if the vector was empty before the addition (`\old(this.size()) == 0`). If it was, the first element should now be the appended element (`this.get(0).equals(e)`). If the vector was not empty, the first element should remain unchanged. However, since the comment specifically mentions the first position containing the appended element, we can infer that the intention is to check the first position only when the vector was initially empty. Therefore, the assertion reflects this condition.
